<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>News from Europe - Latest world headlines and daily news - France 24</title><subtitle type="html">FRANCE 24 explores events across Europe, including in the 27 member states of the European Union and the United Kingdom. Follow our on-the-ground reports, interviews and analyses of the events affecting social and political life on the Continent and Europe’s role in the world.</subtitle><id>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/rss</id><updated>2026-11-25T00:56:08Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/rss" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>Russian nuclear satellites plan 'foolhardy', expert says</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:eaf0837f53bafff9128522242cc3b7cdb622a0e96f3bdd7bdb028e6222d227da</id><updated>2026-11-25T00:55:47Z</updated><published>2026-11-24T20:31:17Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/russian-nuclear-satellites-plan-foolhardy-expert-says--a17887817d5f.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/russian-nuclear-satellites-plan-foolhardy-expert-says" /><summary type="html">NATO chief Mark Rutte said Monday the alliance would defend against threats in space when asked about German media reports that Russia may be preparing to launch a nuclear-armed satellite. Speaking with FRANCE 24's Jennie Shin, Dafydd Townley, Senior Teaching Fellow in International Security at the University of Portsmouth, says that the alleged plan would be "foolhardy because the impact would be indiscriminate, they wouldn't be able to choose only Western or non-Russian satellites".</summary></entry><entry><title>Russian losses on Ukrainian front top 700,000 including missing</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a1d5175f0d8594e449f2a1234c912a6388073dfcd0199be4aac1586488bf324c</id><updated>2026-11-25T00:56:02Z</updated><published>2026-11-24T19:22:31Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/russian-losses-on-ukrainian-front-top-700-000-including-missing--6a745520bcf6.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/russian-losses-on-ukrainian-front-top-700-000-including-missing" /><summary type="html">New analysis of leaked Russian government data suggests more than 700,000 Russian soldiers have died in the war against Ukraine. Independent Russian media outlets have updated their estimates of Moscow's military casualties, including soldiers missing on the frontline, after Belarusian and Ukrainian hackers obtained figures from the Russian statistics agency. FRANCE 24's Carys Garland explains.</summary></entry><entry><title>Russia's war on Ukraine: 'Both sides are prepared to operate outside of the conflict zone'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:71f0bb454d8938d49e21a9c6a3fa9aa50a682458cb247a034010bf2936c5bfad</id><updated>2026-11-25T00:56:08Z</updated><published>2026-11-24T17:26:47Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/russia-s-war-on-ukraine-both-sides-are-prepared-to-operate-outside-of-the-conflict-zone--766d3b319486.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/russia-s-war-on-ukraine-both-sides-are-prepared-to-operate-outside-of-the-conflict-zone" /><summary type="html">Charli James is pleased to welcome Gavin Hall, Teaching Fellow in Political Science, and International Security at the University of Strathclyde. Hall examines recent Russian and Ukrainian operations beyond the main conflict zone, the conditions necessary for a negotiated settlement and the implications of diminishing direct US military support for Ukraine. “Both sides are prepared to operate beyond the main battleground and outside of the conflict zone,” he explains. Hall discusses why both sides want to negotiate from a position of strength and the conditions under which a “mutually hurting stalemate” could lead to a negotiated settlement.</summary></entry><entry><title>Live: Putin says Ukraine still hits Russian oil plants despite Trump's requests to stop</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:20ed5a5645739b074444aa2078e6f72c68705a62f51d086fdf0d548ab3261610</id><updated>2026-11-25T00:54:34Z</updated><published>2026-11-24T05:50:16Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20261124-live-tripoli-demands-explanation-from-kyiv-for-striking-russian-ships-in-libyan-waters--e55baa58ddf4.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261124-live-tripoli-demands-explanation-from-kyiv-for-striking-russian-ships-in-libyan-waters" /><summary type="html">Ukraine continues attacks on Russian oil refineries despite requests from US President ​Donald Trump to ‌withhold them, Russian leader Vladimir Putin said Tuesday, pledging to ⁠retaliate. Kyiv has said it would not stop targeting Russian energy targets until Moscow had done the same. Follow our liveblog for all the latest updates.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Zelensky urges four-way peace talks with Russia, Europe and US 'as soon as possible'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:43b4e07cd0c74f4ba98297d82efc7f022c94f9f08d1e4c0da52dd0f4b5dcf1c9</id><updated>2026-11-25T00:54:34Z</updated><published>2026-11-24T00:30:11Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20261124-zelensky-urges-four-way-peace-talks-with-russia-europe-and-us-as-soon-as-possible--354e3c5e6ad8.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261124-zelensky-urges-four-way-peace-talks-with-russia-europe-and-us-as-soon-as-possible" /><summary type="html">Ukrainian President Volodymyr Zelensky is calling for a new round of negotiations involving Ukraine, Russia, the United States and European leaders, saying Kyiv is ready to meet as early as Tuesday.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>NATO vows space defence after Russia nuclear satellite report</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:46212584cdad6ab6909c10d4f503da5db0a65f85278331f0cca36cccf331b3b3</id><updated>2026-11-25T00:54:34Z</updated><published>2026-11-23T22:33:03Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/nato-vows-space-defence-after-russia-nuclear-satellite-report--b818d8d38eb9.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/nato-vows-space-defence-after-russia-nuclear-satellite-report" /><summary type="html">NATO chief Mark Rutte said Monday the alliance would defend against threats in space when asked about German media reports that Russia may be preparing to launch a nuclear-armed satellite. The media reports, citing unnamed German military and BND spy agency sources, said Moscow was thought to be planning such a launch in the coming weeks, giving it the capability to destroy other satellites. FRANCE 24's Laurent Berstecher reports.</summary></entry><entry><title>Ukraine: 'A war of unmanned machines, AI and total transparency of the battlefield'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:2cd15502ebc9c1d40c40d5f5c7cd9f4e2932e559e3b4fa332a0c6c7c2b1acc80</id><updated>2026-11-25T00:54:34Z</updated><published>2026-11-23T21:56:25Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/a-propos/20261123-a-war-of-unmanned-machines-ai-and-total-transparency-of-the-battlefield--b335b8ca1842.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/a-propos/20261123-a-war-of-unmanned-machines-ai-and-total-transparency-of-the-battlefield" /><summary type="html">Speaking with FRANCE 24's Sharon Gaffney, Nobel Peace Prize laureate Oleksandra Matviichuk, Director of the Centre for Civil Liberties, says that today's war in Ukraine "is a war of unmanned machines, AI, total transparency of the battlefield, mass drone attacks and long-range weapons, and this means we have to rethink how to protect human beings".</summary><category term="A propos" /></entry><entry><title>Ukraine: 'A war of unmanned machines, AI and total transparency of the battlefield'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:8adb09184945de3e75bfb16c5a260fd784cefa899d6fe5fe94333efc57056d76</id><updated>2026-11-25T00:54:34Z</updated><published>2026-11-23T21:54:56Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/a-war-of-unmanned-machines-ai-and-total-transparency-of-the-battlefield--4945328f5666.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/a-war-of-unmanned-machines-ai-and-total-transparency-of-the-battlefield" /><summary type="html">Speaking with FRANCE 24's Sharon Gaffney, Nobel Peace Prize laureate Oleksandra Matviichuk, Director of the Centre for Civil Liberties, says that today's war in Ukraine "is a war of unmanned machines, AI, total transparency of the battlefield, mass drone attacks and long-range weapons, and this means we have to rethink how to protect human beings".</summary></entry><entry><title>Libya's east seeks UN probe into claims Ukrainian military present in west</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:bd2252ac1b20ebd7bedb62eba41411b60efdd7a17ba62c60a3e4153b615641a2</id><updated>2026-11-25T00:54:34Z</updated><published>2026-11-23T20:08:10Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/libya-s-east-seeks-un-probe-into-claims-ukrainian-military-present-in-west--6cb055560ea5.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/libya-s-east-seeks-un-probe-into-claims-ukrainian-military-present-in-west" /><summary type="html">Authorities in divided Libya's east called on Monday for the United Nations to investigate claims that Ukrainian forces were present in the country's west, as they lodged a complaint over Ukrainian attacks on two Russian ships off Benghazi. The strikes on Sunday, claimed by Kyiv, come as Ukraine steps up strikes against Russia far from the front lines of their war. FRANCE 24's Emerald Maxwell reports.</summary></entry><entry><title>Ukraine claims it sank Russian warship off Libya</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:1335987e61b434f0740997d307b5db836b953a749d86f258e07fe423fd0f4bd2</id><updated>2026-11-25T00:54:34Z</updated><published>2026-11-23T19:39:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/ukraine-claims-it-sank-russian-warship-off-libya--1e8645cf71f5.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/ukraine-claims-it-sank-russian-warship-off-libya" /><summary type="html">Ukraine on Monday claimed it was behind strikes on two Russian vessels off Libya, including one that sank a modern warship, in the latest spillover from Moscow's invasion. The attacks on Sunday near the Libyan port of Benghazi come at a time when Ukraine has stepped up its daring strikes against Russia far from the frontlines in retaliation for Moscow's deadly invasion. FRANCE 24's Gulliver Cragg reports from Kyiv.</summary></entry><entry><title>Finland summons Russian ambassador after suspected airspace violation</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:287ab237d3985421b6f73a511dad74c950d4414ed8489e1fd4b55ddce77ae679</id><updated>2026-11-25T00:54:34Z</updated><published>2026-11-23T16:50:41Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20261123-finland-summons-russian-ambassador-after-suspected-airspace-violation--777165c768bd.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261123-finland-summons-russian-ambassador-after-suspected-airspace-violation" /><summary type="html">Finland on Monday said it had summoned Russia's ambassador over a suspected violation of Finnish airspace by a Russian helicopter and after a Ukrainian drone strike on a Russian cargo ship located in the Gulf of Finland in recent days. Helsinki also condemned Moscow's escalating strikes on civilian targets in Ukraine.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>12,000 evacuated from Don Toliver concert after unknown substance sickens fans</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:d96b09dc7346cbc823567652d5d52435748b78cd660ec6d222e1f329d4d386f9</id><updated>2026-11-25T00:54:34Z</updated><published>2026-11-23T15:46:48Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261123-12-000-evacuated-from-don-toliver-concert-after-unknown-substance-sickens-fans--c4a2bcadc8d2.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261123-12-000-evacuated-from-don-toliver-concert-after-unknown-substance-sickens-fans" /><summary type="html">More than 12,000 fans were evacuated from a concert by American rapper Don Toliver and over 80 were treated by medics after an unknown irritant was released in the crowd, authorities in the English city of Manchester said Monday.</summary></entry><entry><title>Ukraine claims strikes on Russian ships off Libyan coast</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a15c17dd656e89574ac1b3f2a258eee4ec20858a038b872ecf7139b72834f58f</id><updated>2026-11-25T00:54:34Z</updated><published>2026-11-23T14:36:26Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261123-ukraine-claims-strikes-on-russian-ships-off-libyan-coast--c6da19d54d8f.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261123-ukraine-claims-strikes-on-russian-ships-off-libyan-coast" /><summary type="html">Ukraine claimed responsibility on Monday for attacks on two Russian vessels off the coast of Libya the previous day. Here is what we know about the operation, claimed by President Volodymyr Zelensky shortly after the United Nations called for an investigation into the strikes.</summary></entry><entry><title>Libya demands answers from Kyiv over drone attack on Russian ships off Benghazi</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:2754e8c21871c3671b406d9f894554b110327c8423052973876dd6fb7ac8251a</id><updated>2026-11-25T00:54:34Z</updated><published>2026-11-23T06:10:26Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20261123-live-russian-strikes-kill-at-least-15-people-in-kyiv-region-ukraine-says--3314f31f0d59.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261123-live-russian-strikes-kill-at-least-15-people-in-kyiv-region-ukraine-says" /><summary type="html">Libya's Tripoli-based government on Monday condemned Ukraine's strikes on two Russian vessels near the eastern city of Benghazi carried out by Ukraine on Sunday. It demanded an explanation from Kyiv, warning that Libya would not be dragged into the war between Russia and Ukraine. Read our live blog to see how the day's events unfolded.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Burnham, 'Brejoin' &amp; the ghosts of Brexit</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:27707729c5729cd45b0eddf5b9f1511bd946c526f4cd4b1e98ec6950b77609b0</id><updated>2026-11-25T00:54:34Z</updated><published>2026-11-22T19:37:13Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/spotlight/20261122-burnham-brejoin-the-ghosts-of-brexit--b3f015196424.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/spotlight/20261122-burnham-brejoin-the-ghosts-of-brexit" /><summary type="html">"The people of Britain have spoken, and the answer is: we are out." Those were the words of David Dimbleby at 4:40am on June 24, 2016, as the Brexit referendum result became clear. But nearly a decade on, is Britain changing its mind? Prime Minister Andy Burnham has reopened talks with Brussels, exploring options for a closer relationship with the EU. The move has, however, drawn criticism from key figures behind Brexit, including Theresa May and Boris Johnson. What is driving this rethink and where might it lead? FRANCE 24's Gavin Lee speaks to John McTernan, veteran Labour strategist and former adviser to Tony Blair.</summary><category term="Spotlight" /></entry><entry><title>Europe sees new protests over rising costs, inequality and public services</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:f779439fe5d88ab06f1f1c5bc775e9cb89220a5240e819ea27ed1feafec15056</id><updated>2026-11-25T00:54:34Z</updated><published>2026-11-22T09:41:29Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe-sees-new-protests-over-rising-costs-inequality-and-public-services--a1d144e53fad.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe-sees-new-protests-over-rising-costs-inequality-and-public-services" /><summary type="html">Sunday marks the third consecutive day of protests across Europe, following large demonstrations on Friday and smaller rallies on Saturday, from Portugal to France. The protests have largely focused on the rising cost of living and access to affordable housing. In France, demonstrations have now taken place for six weekends in a row. Ophelie Jacobson reports.</summary></entry><entry><title>Ukrainian rescuers search for survivors in rubble after Russian attack</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:185963357f0556cc78353eb11c6b97fe965ee6c98657c33a2fcff4f2f4367a95</id><updated>2026-11-25T00:54:34Z</updated><published>2026-11-22T06:15:38Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20261122-live-finland-says-war-spilling-over-after-baltic-sea-drone-strike-on-russian-cargo-ship--98ee191af9fb.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261122-live-finland-says-war-spilling-over-after-baltic-sea-drone-strike-on-russian-cargo-ship" /><summary type="html">Ukrainian rescue teams on Sunday searched for survivors in the rubble of a collapsed residential building in Dymer, in the Kyiv region, after a Russian drone strike, which killed two people and wounded four others. Meanwhile, Finland warned the war was "spilling over" after a drone set fire to a Russian cargo ship in the Baltic Sea Saturday. Read our blog to see how the day's events unfolded.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>EU-Indonesia agreement sees the light after ten years of negotiations</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:01f3dfe2f8319e496731d380b39278c16b9b3dcbe31ad90e522e4ccc2751195b</id><updated>2026-11-25T00:54:34Z</updated><published>2026-11-21T22:23:03Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261121-eu-indonesia-agreement-sees-the-light-after-ten-years-of-negotiations--6b9c7be2271c.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261121-eu-indonesia-agreement-sees-the-light-after-ten-years-of-negotiations" /><summary type="html">The European Union and Indonesia have signed a major trade deal, ten years after talks began.The agreement removes almost all tariffs between the EU and Southeast Asia's biggest economy: 98.5 per cent of them. For Europe, it means access to a market of 280 million people and a steadier supply of nickel for batteries. For Indonesia, easier exports of palm oil, textiles and footwear, and it arrives just before its current EU trade preferences end on the 1st of January. To discuss the deal Airlangga Hartarto, Coordinating Minister for Economic Affairs in Indonesia joined us on the programme.</summary></entry><entry><title>Russia attacks Zelensky's hometown, Ukraine reaffirms wish to join NATO</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:000afd0df7e691a35a10a59d8077946f61d2dcf929d51f34e4bfb93888cfc197</id><updated>2026-11-25T00:54:34Z</updated><published>2026-11-21T19:56:39Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20261121-russia-attacks-zelensky-s-hometown-ukraine-reaffirms-wish-to-join-nato--7bb8a856bfbd.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261121-russia-attacks-zelensky-s-hometown-ukraine-reaffirms-wish-to-join-nato" /><summary type="html">A Russian ballistic missile attack on President Volodymyr Zelensky’s hometown in central Ukraine on Saturday killed two people and wounded dozens. Hours later, Zelensky reiterated his country's determination to join NATO, following proposals to provide Kyiv with security guarantees similar to those of the military alliance.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Russia launches ballistic missile attack on Zelensky's hometown in central Ukraine</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b553c8eea4ee4ce7105ac3b78297bb2437480aa4351aef084fe3b5f4f5457f48</id><updated>2026-11-25T00:54:34Z</updated><published>2026-11-21T19:55:07Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/russia-launches-ballistic-missile-attack-on-zelensky-s-hometown-in-central-ukraine--9ccdbee28248.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/russia-launches-ballistic-missile-attack-on-zelensky-s-hometown-in-central-ukraine" /><summary type="html">A Russian ballistic missile attack on President Volodymyr Zelensky’s hometown in central Ukraine on Saturday killed two people and wounded dozens. Hours later, Zelensky reiterated his country's determination to join NATO. FRANCE 24's Gulliver Cragg reports from Kyiv.</summary></entry><entry><title>Drone attack sets Russian cargo ship ablaze in Gulf of Finland</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:5651baa90aea88fed148a6d07e5d0b48b79f090a800309efdc59038b2d0646dd</id><updated>2026-11-25T00:54:34Z</updated><published>2026-11-21T18:02:23Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/drone-attack-sets-russian-cargo-ship-ablaze-in-gulf-of-finland--6ddedb55210c.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/drone-attack-sets-russian-cargo-ship-ablaze-in-gulf-of-finland" /><summary type="html">A Russian cargo ship caught fire after ​being hit by drones in the Baltic Sea on Saturday and drifted into Finnish waters. Reporting from Kyiv, FRANCE 24's Gulliver Cragg notes that the ship is affiliated with a major Russian military logistics company. While Ukrainian authorities typically neither confirm nor deny responsibility, analysts cite a clear motive for the targeting, Cragg explains.</summary></entry><entry><title>Drone attack sets Russian cargo ship ablaze in Gulf of Finland</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:fe636a668ab0927c0acec44878e95da01dc517799ef459f4fcbe1cdee6e382a3</id><updated>2026-11-25T00:54:34Z</updated><published>2026-11-21T12:35:54Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20261121-drone-attack-sets-russian-cargo-ship-ablaze-in-gulf-of-finland--c7c9c4110e34.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261121-drone-attack-sets-russian-cargo-ship-ablaze-in-gulf-of-finland" /><summary type="html">A Russian cargo ship caught fire after a drone strike in international waters in the Gulf of Finland on Saturday and later drifted into the country's ⁠territorial waters, Finnish authorities said. Helsinki alerted NATO and imposed temporary restrictions in the area amid heightened tensions in the Baltic Sea.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>'Accept cookies'? Russia collects data from swaths of unknowing Swedes</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:5ccfa0a71065bfefaa3c4ec601141f4cccd0cad0262eff877d6eb7efe8ef33ac</id><updated>2026-11-25T00:54:34Z</updated><published>2026-11-21T10:55:32Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20261121-accept-cookies-russia-collected-data-swaths-unknowing-swedes--a6892ead2cc3.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261121-accept-cookies-russia-collected-data-swaths-unknowing-swedes" /><summary type="html">A Russian tech firm backed by an oligarch close to President Vladimir Putin has secretly been collecting data from hundreds of thousands – possibly millions – of Swedes, a newspaper investigation found. The revelation has rattled the Nordic nation, whose proximity to Russia and unusually open public records system make it particularly vulnerable to Moscow’s hybrid war tactics.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>'Unacceptable': EU chief condemns alleged Russian plot to kill US-Ukrainian citizen</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:7d6319b9128cc2b302e73f886fd077cd67fd1db374e684883e6ca5227c573b5b</id><updated>2026-11-25T00:54:34Z</updated><published>2026-11-21T10:32:36Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20261121-unacceptable-eu-chief-condemns-alleged-russian-plot-to-kill-us-ukrainian-citizen--dca3e06988cd.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261121-unacceptable-eu-chief-condemns-alleged-russian-plot-to-kill-us-ukrainian-citizen" /><summary type="html">European Commission President Ursula von der Leyen condemned an alleged Russian intelligence plot to assassinate a US-Ukrainian citizen in Denmark, vowing full solidarity with Copenhagen.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>EU, UK reach reset deal after Brexit</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:8eccfa483ccdc16b582b11ba0d24fdef54807372d3a644cc1b691b3a400f7434</id><updated>2026-11-25T00:54:34Z</updated><published>2026-11-21T09:43:42Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/eu-uk-reach-reset-deal-after-brexit--3244a7b00c69.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/eu-uk-reach-reset-deal-after-brexit" /><summary type="html">The UK and the EU signed three agreements on Friday at a summit in Brussels, marking a new effort to reset post-Brexit relations. The deals aim to reduce red tape for food exports, link emissions trading schemes and allow tens of thousands of young people to live and work more freely across the Channel. Prime Minister Andy Burnham has called Brexit an “obvious failure” to deliver on its promises and wants to deepen ties with the EU, a position criticised by veteran Brexiteer Nigel Farage, who has warned of a political backlash. Daniel Quinlan has this story.</summary></entry><entry><title>UK and EU strike ‘landmark’ deal to rebuild ties after Brexit</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:12fd8c7cbfea0fe004dbc6d9b013fa696071327b8c9de4319857b78cbf9ed8be</id><updated>2026-11-25T00:54:34Z</updated><published>2026-11-20T17:06:59Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261120-uk-and-eu-strike-landmark-deal-to-rebuild-ties-after-brexit--fb622c5a1ee8.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261120-uk-and-eu-strike-landmark-deal-to-rebuild-ties-after-brexit" /><summary type="html">🇬🇧🇪🇺 A fresh start after #Brexit? The #UK and #EU have agreed on a landmark #deal to rebuild ties, following a summit in Brussels this Friday. The agreement covers easier food export checks, youth mobility and carbon emission quotas.</summary></entry><entry><title>‘A more expensive EU is not a better EU’: Austria's Minister for Europe, Claudia Bauer</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:823b68de0a0672b459a95020ca6aad9cb1f4a7f4526f645b378feddfb5421f90</id><updated>2026-11-25T00:54:34Z</updated><published>2026-11-20T16:53:27Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/talking-europe/20261120-a-more-expensive-eu-is-not-a-better-eu-austria-s-minister-for-europe-claudia-bauer--aeea629ca19f.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/talking-europe/20261120-a-more-expensive-eu-is-not-a-better-eu-austria-s-minister-for-europe-claudia-bauer" /><summary type="html">This week's programme hosted Claudia Bauer, Austria’s Federal Minister for Europe, Integration and Family while she was in Paris for the recent G7 meeting. She offered her thoughts on the diplomatic moves surrounding Ukraine, transatlantic relations, EU enlargement and a headscarf ban in Austrian schools that has caused disquiet. We also talked about the thorny negotiations involved in the EU’s next long-term budget: the Multiannual Financial Framework.</summary><category term="Talking Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Spain’s political crossroads, Europe’s wider stakes: Spaniards to vote in key election</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:7b0ecba7cdac86ccf75d0baf500fd210f169be91e42656a72913244dc5cbf925</id><updated>2026-11-25T00:54:34Z</updated><published>2026-11-20T15:17:17Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/talking-europe/20261120-spains-political-crossroads-europes-wider-stakes-spaniards-to-vote-in-key-election--45b0fdce8813.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/talking-europe/20261120-spains-political-crossroads-europes-wider-stakes-spaniards-to-vote-in-key-election" /><summary type="html">The stakes are high – not only for people in Spain, but also for Europe. On November 29, the country holds a parliamentary election that could see the end of the Socialist-led government and potentially a coalition between the right and the far right, in one of the EU’s biggest and most influential member states. It could also signal the end of Pedro Sanchez’s third term in office. Among other things, the prime minister may pay the political price for two shocking train crashes and the migrant crisis in Spain’s North African exclave of Ceuta.</summary><category term="Talking Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Does staggered consent actually protect young people?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:1e542159c3ba01dd84f742d0234b654f0fb213f8f84505d4ddc3a1e32b5b99be</id><updated>2026-11-25T00:54:34Z</updated><published>2026-11-20T14:14:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/the-51/20261120-does-staggered-consent-actually-protect-young-people--b74fdbb9cde1.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/the-51/20261120-does-staggered-consent-actually-protect-young-people" /><summary type="html">Following recent scandals involving two iconic British comedians, the UK government is considering the introduction of staggered age consent. Annette Young talks to Katherine Allen from the Institute of Social Justice and Crime in the UK about whether such laws work. Also the social costs of femicide; how do loved ones cope with such a loss, and what support is available to families in the wake of such a tragedy? Plus we meet the women who are challenging the traditions of Mexican mariachi music, a world that remains largely male dominated.</summary><category term="The 51%" /></entry><entry><title>Poland slams Russian 'provocation' as missiles land near European military drills</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:62b2caa583753c64fd4c039322f9a498092c3c48539b498bf50dba74e3a4dadf</id><updated>2026-11-25T00:54:34Z</updated><published>2026-11-20T10:38:51Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20261120-poland-says-russian-missile-hit-its-territory-during-attack-on-ukraine--6a169bd9648e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261120-poland-says-russian-missile-hit-its-territory-during-attack-on-ukraine" /><summary type="html">Two Russian missiles and a suspected drone came down in Poland on Friday in what Prime Minister Donald Tusk said was likely an "intentional provocation" timed to coincide with European military exercises in the country for a possible postwar mission in Ukraine.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry></feed>
